  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(m)$ be some function such that $f(m)\\to \\infty$ as $m\\to \\infty$. Does there exist a graph $G$ of infinite chromatic number such that every subgraph on $m$ vertices contains an independent set of size at least $\\frac{m}{2}-f(m)$?",
